# Harbor safety

## Gate

Load on every Harbor turn. Skip only when the turn never touches Harbor
projects, artifacts, retention, or robots.

## Read-only default

List projects, repos, and artifacts are fine when Harbor work is
authorized. Do **not**:

- delete an artifact, tag, repository, or project
- run retention that purges tags the user did not name or authorize
- create a robot account and paste its secret/token into chat
- broaden project member roles or flip visibility to public

…unless the user gave an **explicit verb this turn naming the object**.

## Mutate gates

| Action | Require |
| --- | --- |
| Delete tag / artifact | delete / remove + project + repo + tag/digest |
| Delete repository | delete / remove + project + repo |
| Delete project | delete / destroy + project (prefer narrower first) |
| Retention policy run / purge | retention / purge / expire + project (+ policy name) |
| Create robot | create robot + project + name; **never** paste the secret |
| Member role widen / public | explicit ACL / public verb + project |

Prefer the narrowest action:

1. Tag/artifact delete over repo wipe
2. Repo delete over project wipe
3. Retention scoped to named tags/rules over "delete everything old"

Ambiguous mass-delete or retention → **ask once** to scope before acting.

## Refuse secrets

Do **not** paste into chat:

- Robot account tokens / secrets
- Admin passwords, OIDC client secrets, or API tokens
- Full vulnerability payloads that embed credentials

Prefer: project/repo/tag **names**, digest prefixes, scan **severity
counts**, and "robot secret was shown once in UI — store in a secret
store" language. If a create-robot response includes a secret, tell the
operator to copy it into a secret store and **do not** repeat it in chat.

## No invented MCP tools

No Harbor MCP was discovered in the live harness catalog. Do not invent
MCP tool names for delete/retention/robot. Use API/UI paths the operator
authorized. If an MCP appears later, use only tools on the live map and
still apply these gates.

## Operator receipt (mutate)

Safe shape:

- Base URL product host (no credentials)
- Project (+ repository / tag when relevant)
- Action taken
- "No robot tokens or admin passwords shown"

